   CPWATCH 4.3                - 11 -           02 December 1984

1  CPWATCH                                          MAINTENANCE
0                          MAINTENANCE
+                          ___________

-  CPWATCH normally only needs maintenance  when there has been
   a  change  in  one  of the  key  control  blocks:  RDEVBLOK,
   VDEVBLOK,  VMBLOK or  PSA are  the usual  ones. The  modules
   which may be affected are:
        CPWDEV
        CPWMAN
        CPWSYS
        CPWUSR
   Normally all that  is required is re-assembly  of these mod-
   ules with the appropriate MACLIBs from CP
0     When this happens, the following  procedure will keep the
   object code separate, and enable  automatic selection of the
   correct object decks:
0       1 Create a  CNTRL and set of  AUXfile names, using
+       1
             naming  conventions consistent  with  CPWATCH
             and CP.  Clone  the CNTRL file from  the next
             level back  of the same  series; add  the AUX
             file ahead of all the others.
0       2 Add a single update  entry to the AUXfile, again
+       2
             borrowing naming conventions from CP.
0       3  Create the  update  files  initially as  single
+       3
             "comment" updates:
             ./  *  DUMMY  UPDATE  TO  FORCE  CREATION  OF
             TXTFILE LEVEL
0       4 Create a new entry  in CPWLVL DATA for automatic
+       4
             selection of the CNTRL file:
             CPWLVL WRITE  xxxxxx ... where xxxxxx  is the
             name of the CNTRL file created.
0       5 Reassemble the affected modules.
+       5
                 VMFASM CPWyyy xxxxxx
             Note that CPWDEV and  CPWUSR normally are the
             ones  that need  re-assembly  - the  RDEVBLOK
             always gets bigger, and both are impacted.
+            ______
0     The following  outlines the work necessary.   The entries
   marked with "*" are supplied pre-assembled.
0  System    Release   Control   MACLIBS   Modules
                       File                Requiring
                                           Re-Assembly
   VM/370    6.0       CPWR6     CPWMAC    CPWSYS
                                 DMKAMAC   CPWUSR
                                 DMKMAC    CPWMAN
                                           CPWDEV
0  BSEPP     2.0       CPWBSE    CPWMAC    CPWSYS
